cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite the accepted DICTA 2026 paper below and identify the software version used. This is the v1.0.5 verification package; the paper-cited v1.0.4 snapshot remains unchanged. Final paper proceedings metadata is pending."
type: software
abstract: >-
  Code and retained numerical evidence for the accepted DICTA 2026 study of
  checkpoint-resolution alignment in frozen vision-language checkpoints on
  Oxford-IIIT-Pet classification and Flickr30k retrieval. Version 1.0.5 adds
  the final exploratory BLIP top-five diagnostic and automated CPU analysis
  verification. Canonical measurements and the paper-cited v1.0.4 snapshot
  are unchanged. Replaying saved statistics does not repeat GPU inference
  or establish the causal mechanism of task-dependent resolution effects.
keywords:
  - vision-language models
  - inference resolution
  - reproducibility
  - measurement study
title: "Testing Checkpoint–Resolution Alignment in Frozen Dual-Embedding Vision–Language Checkpoints: Accuracy and Recorded-Protocol Costs"
authors:
